skills/manuscript-journal-adapt/references/llm-smells.md and humanize-contract.md adapt patterns, rules and
process steps from the following MIT-licensed projects. The text and examples here are rewritten for
scientific manuscripts; detector-evasion techniques from these projects are deliberately not included.

- humanizer, https://github.com/blader/humanizer
  Copyright (c) 2025 Siqi Chen. MIT License.
  Its pattern catalogue is based on Wikipedia's "Signs of AI writing" (WikiProject AI Cleanup).

- humanize, https://github.com/harshaneel/humanize
  Copyright (c) 2026 Harshaneel Gokhale. MIT License.
  Adapted: editing levers 3 to 8, the rhetorical-scaffolding checklist, the literal pre-output gate and the
  writer-profile step. Not adapted: perplexity injection, burstiness targets, RLHF-voice stripping,
  detector-scored selection and paraphrase passes.

skills/manuscript-integrity-check/references/kobak_2024_style_words.csv is recomputed from the yearly word
counts published by Kobak et al. (Science Advances 11(27):eadt3813, 2025;
https://github.com/berenslab/llm-excess-vocab) using the paper's published formula.

Ideas, rules and diagnostic tests were also drawn, in paraphrase, from a survey (2026-10-15) of open-source
writing skills, among them: AIScientists-Dev/academic-humanizer, matsuikentaro1/humanizer_academic,
Aperivue/medsci-skills, uchicago-dsi/ai-sci-skills, stephenturner/skill-deslop, labarba/sciwrite (CC BY 4.0),
taehyeonglim/academic-humanizer, Kiterlin/anti-defensive-writing, WantongC/journal-adapt-writing-skill,
K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills, Orchestra-Research/AI-Research-SKILLs, conorbronsdon/avoid-ai-writing,
hardikpandya/stop-slop, Nanako0129/sepia, Aboudjem/humanizer-skill, seyedehsanhadi/sloptrim (Apache-2.0),
mshumer/unslop and eric-tramel/slop-guard (MIT unless noted). No text was copied from sources without a
licence; their ideas are restated in our own words.
